  "problem": "A supplier of clothing materials looks for flaws before selling the material to customers. On average, there have been $1.7$ flaws per meter. What is the probability of finding fewer than $4$  flaws in the next meter length of the material? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that flaws appear independently and at a constant average rate.",
